# Infisical Universal Auth bootstrap credentials.
#
# These are the only variables you provide yourself. Varlock uses them to
# authenticate to the Infisical project. Every other variable lives in
# Infisical and is fetched at dev time, or synced into Vercel at build time,
# so nothing else belongs in this file.
#
# Provide them either by exporting them from your shell (for example from
# `~/.zshenv`) or by copying this file to a local, gitignored `.env`. Then
# start the dev server with `bun run dev`, which runs
# `varlock run -- nuxt dev`.
#
# Create the machine identity in Infisical:
#   Access Control > Machine Identities > Create Identity > Universal Auth
# Grant it read-only access to this project (the built-in Viewer role), then
# copy its Client ID and Client Secret below.
# https://infisical.com/docs/documentation/platform/identities/universal-auth

INFISICAL_CLIENT_ID=""
INFISICAL_CLIENT_SECRET=""
